  "task": "Assess the disaster recovery / resiliency posture of workloads running in the eu-west-1 region.",
  "context": "User wants to know how well their eu-west-1 workloads would survive a disaster (region or AZ loss) and where they currently stand. This is a broad resiliency posture check, not a root-cause investigation into a specific incident.",
  "resources": ["region: eu-west-1", "all AWS accounts associated with this agent space"],
  "timeframe": "current state (not time-bound)",
  "criteria": "Look for: (1) AWS Resilience Hub (v1 and/or v2/NGRH) applications and assessments scoped to eu-west-1 — resiliency scores, RTO/RPO targets vs actuals, outstanding resiliency recommendations; (2) Multi-AZ configuration for key stateful resources (RDS/Aurora, ElastiCache, EFS) and compute (ASGs, EKS node groups) in eu-west-1; (3) AWS Backup coverage — vaults, plans, retention, and recovery points for eu-west-1 resources; (4) Cross-region DR posture — S3 cross-region replication, RDS cross-region read replicas, DynamoDB global tables, or any secondary/standby region paired with eu-west-1; (5) Any single points of failure (single-AZ resources, no backups configured). Summarize overall maturity/gaps rather than dumping raw resource lists."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Assess disaster recovery posture for eu-west-1 workloads"}], "created_at": null}

